Data scope and attribution
==========================

The software license in LICENSE does not license external research data.
This revision contains vehicle-role metadata and aggregate verification tables,
but not the original mobility trace, prepared report arrays, radio maps,
per-window prediction archives or trained checkpoints.

The mobility source used in the study is TAPASCologne, credited to Sandesh
Uppoor, Diala Naboulsi and Marco Fiore:
http://kolntrace.project.citi-lab.fr/

The study's existing data documentation identifies the mobility-derived data as
CC BY-NC. This source-code reorganization does not change those terms or grant
additional redistribution rights. Obtain the original trace from its provider
and consult the terms accompanying the particular data artifact you use.
The synthetic radio layer was generated using Sionna RT and scene geometry;
source-code availability does not imply redistribution of the underlying scene.

Vehicle identifiers in configs/vehicle_roles.json and the aggregate tables are
study metadata. Any separately released data archive must carry its own source
attribution, contents manifest and applicable usage terms. No new data-release
permission or public download location is established by this revision.
